      {
        "key": "doc:synthetic-catalog",
        "path": "/synthetic/catalog.md",
        "content": "# Warehouse catalog\n\nSKU-4711 is a stainless steel flange sold in packs of twelve. It ships from the Rotterdam facility and is stocked in aisle fourteen. Replacement gaskets are ordered separately under the accessories catalog, and the pack size cannot be split across two orders.\n"
      },
      {
        "key": "doc:synthetic-invoice",
        "path": "/synthetic/invoice.md",
        "content": "# Invoice archive\n\nINVOICE-90210 covers the third-quarter licence renewal and was settled by bank transfer. The archive keeps one entry per settled invoice, recording the settlement date, the paying entity and the reference the bank returned.\n"
      },
      {
        "key": "doc:synthetic-incident",
        "path": "/synthetic/incident.md",
        "content": "# Incident record\n\nINC-2291 describes a partial loss of write availability in the primary region. The trigger was an exhausted connection pool; the mitigation was to raise the pool ceiling and shed background traffic until the backlog had drained.\n"
      },
      {
        "key": "doc:synthetic-runbook",
        "path": "/synthetic/runbook.md",
        "content": "# Failover runbook\n\nRUNBOOK-ZEPHYR is the procedure for draining a region before planned maintenance. It covers quiescing the queue workers, promoting the standby replica, and confirming that no lease is still held when the switch is thrown.\n"
      },
      {
        "key": "doc:synthetic-datasheet",
        "path": "/synthetic/datasheet.md",
        "content": "# Component datasheet\n\nPart MX-88Q is a temperature-compensated pressure transducer rated for continuous duty. Its calibration interval is twelve months and its output is a four to twenty milliampere current loop.\n"
      },
      {
        "key": "doc:synthetic-contract",
        "path": "/synthetic/contract.md",
        "content": "# Contract register\n\nCTR-5150 is the master services agreement covering managed hosting. Its renewal clause is automatic unless either party gives ninety days of written notice, and its liability cap is stated per incident rather than per year.\n"
      },
      {
        "key": "doc:synthetic-release",
        "path": "/synthetic/release.md",
        "content": "# Release notes\n\nBuild orion-r7 ships the queue-draining fix and a faster startup path for the worker pool. Operators upgrading from an earlier build should expect one extra restart while the new lease format is adopted.\n"
      },
      {
        "key": "doc:synthetic-telemetry",
        "path": "/synthetic/telemetry.md",
        "content": "# Telemetry alerts\n\nTELEMETRY_LAG_HIGH fires when the ingestion pipeline falls more than five minutes behind the producing edge. The alert clears on its own once the backlog drains, and a sustained firing points at a saturated consumer rather than a slow producer.\n"
      },
      {
        "key": "doc:synthetic-warehouse",
        "path": "/synthetic/warehouse.md",
        "content": "# Facility register\n\nWH-ROT-02 is the secondary distribution facility, with a bonded storage area and a dedicated returns dock. Night shifts run Monday to Thursday, and cross-docked freight is never held overnight.\n"
      },
      {
        "key": "doc:synthetic-onboarding",
        "path": "/synthetic/onboarding.md",
        "content": "# Onboarding checklist\n\nOB-3310 is the checklist a new field technician completes before the first unaccompanied call. It covers tooling issue, the safety briefing, vehicle assignment and the sign-off the supervising technician records.\n"
      }
    ],
